WEBVTT

00:00:00.152 --> 00:00:05.716
Night fog at the Southampton port.

00:00:11.397 --> 00:00:18.507
After parting from mr. Carson and his children,
Candy went towards the port in Southampton.

00:00:21.266 --> 00:00:25.950
In order to help Candy on her way to America,
mr. Carson wrote a letter of introduction...

00:00:26.103 --> 00:00:31.255
...to his friend, who runs a shipping company.

00:00:47.114 --> 00:00:51.718
Kurin, this is Southampton port.
Terry departed to America from this place.

00:00:53.212 --> 00:00:56.700
Now... let's find mr. Carson's friend
and his shipping company.

00:01:05.635 --> 00:01:09.398
Juskin?
Let's see, do I know that guy...

00:01:09.609 --> 00:01:12.563
-You know him?
-Never heard of him...

00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:16.305
I was told that I'd find him as soon
as I ask around Southampton's port...

00:01:17.374 --> 00:01:20.704
There is a large shipping company that way.
Ask around there.

00:01:20.739 --> 00:01:22.461
-You should do that.
-Thank you.

00:01:44.618 --> 00:01:49.602
I don't think that well-meaning mr. Carson
would've introduced me to a non-existant company.

00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:54.815
Thief!

00:01:56.191 --> 00:01:57.267
Thief?

00:01:57.643 --> 00:01:59.806
Hey, show some respect!

00:02:00.192 --> 00:02:02.318
But that's my trunk!

00:02:02.548 --> 00:02:06.057
I'm working as a luggage carrier in this port.

00:02:06.502 --> 00:02:07.750
Working?

00:02:08.183 --> 00:02:11.321
I'm sorry, but I have no money to pay you.

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:12.870
Cheapskate.

00:02:13.034 --> 00:02:16.989
Hey, you, I already told you that I'm broke!

00:02:17.258 --> 00:02:21.987
Now that I got a hold of your trunk,
you don't get to be stingy anymore!

00:02:22.036 --> 00:02:22.962
I'll carry it!

00:02:23.985 --> 00:02:26.875
Wait!
I'm not going anywhere!

00:02:27.857 --> 00:02:30.024
Don't tell me you're some bum?

00:02:31.044 --> 00:02:35.393
I came looking for Juskin's shipping company,
but I can't seem to find it...

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.426
Juskin?

00:02:38.053 --> 00:02:38.920
You know him?

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.913
I think I saw it written on a billboard somewhere...

00:02:42.074 --> 00:02:44.120
Please, remember!

00:02:45.882 --> 00:02:47.310
Juskin...

00:02:49.049 --> 00:02:50.946
-You remembered?
-Yeah.

00:03:02.976 --> 00:03:06.328
-It's in such a desolate place?
-I'm sure it was around here...

00:03:06.529 --> 00:03:07.511
There it is!

00:03:13.309 --> 00:03:14.696
Juskin.

00:03:16.573 --> 00:03:19.920
-Anyhow, it looks like a horrible company.
-Yes...

00:03:22.458 --> 00:03:23.228
A customer!

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:24.709
See you then!

00:03:24.798 --> 00:03:27.808
-But I need to thank you...
-I got that customer because of you!

00:03:28.002 --> 00:03:28.772
Bye!

00:03:30.215 --> 00:03:31.485
Thank you!

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.643
Maybe this company went broke?

00:03:48.597 --> 00:03:53.082
-One pair... three cards...
-Sorry... full house...!

00:03:56.499 --> 00:03:58.448
-...I give up.
-Yeah...

00:03:58.483 --> 00:03:59.835
Hey, say something!

00:04:00.574 --> 00:04:04.932
-Mr. Juskin! When are we gonna get paid?
-Really!

00:04:05.389 --> 00:04:07.714
You ain't paying us enough!

00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:11.416
Isn't there a way out of this?

00:04:17.661 --> 00:04:22.167
If it's come down to this, we'll have
to sell our children to some foreign country!

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:27.178
Of course, we might even
earn something from them!

00:04:28.316 --> 00:04:30.010
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:04:34.403 --> 00:04:36.514
Ouch...

00:04:37.581 --> 00:04:38.534
Who is that?

00:04:39.315 --> 00:04:42.415
Uh... I... I must have missed a building...

00:04:42.622 --> 00:04:44.627
Who is that girl?

00:04:45.494 --> 00:04:48.073
You've got a nice office there...

00:04:54.414 --> 00:04:55.226
Here.

00:04:57.951 --> 00:05:00.989
Huh? Isn't this letter addressed to me?

00:05:01.757 --> 00:05:03.513
No, that's...

00:05:04.358 --> 00:05:08.824
Carson... who is this Carson guy...

00:05:09.169 --> 00:05:12.752
Uh, I'm sure this is a mistake!
I'll be on my way now...

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.472
Hold on, girl!

00:05:18.245 --> 00:05:19.486
Hey, hold on!

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:24.131
I remembered, I remembered!
I borrowed money from that weirdo, Carson!

00:05:24.166 --> 00:05:25.519
Is he doing well?

00:05:26.147 --> 00:05:27.235
Y..yes...

00:05:27.469 --> 00:05:30.314
Hey, girl, come to our office.

00:05:32.025 --> 00:05:33.494
Welcome, miss!

00:05:34.797 --> 00:05:37.545
So Carson is still the same.

00:05:37.752 --> 00:05:39.294
That's right...

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:42.898
No... I mean...

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.184
By the way, miss, is it true that you
want to go to America?

00:05:46.219 --> 00:05:46.914
Yes...

00:05:48.153 --> 00:05:49.524
To America?

00:05:50.173 --> 00:05:52.363
But I don't want to be sold!

00:05:52.554 --> 00:05:53.766
Sold?

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:04.838
You were eavesdropping on us a little while ago?

00:06:05.112 --> 00:06:09.146
Eavesdropping? You spoke loudly and I heard you!

00:06:09.619 --> 00:06:11.035
I'm going back!

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.539
We were just kidding, right?

00:06:15.022 --> 00:06:18.788
Conversation becomes lighter when we do that.
Right?

00:06:18.823 --> 00:06:20.348
Yeah, it's just a joke.

00:06:20.915 --> 00:06:23.685
Do we look like we're up to
something that bad?

00:06:24.387 --> 00:06:26.568
Here, take a good look into my eyes!

00:06:31.672 --> 00:06:34.820
-Miss, you wanna go to America?
-Yes.

00:06:34.855 --> 00:06:36.162
Leave it to me.

00:06:37.316 --> 00:06:41.531
We'll think of something...
But it won't be easy!

00:06:41.876 --> 00:06:43.450
How much money do you have?

00:06:44.129 --> 00:06:45.547
I don't have any.

00:06:46.536 --> 00:06:50.365
What? What do you mean?
You want to travel to America without a penny?

00:06:52.043 --> 00:06:58.815
Mr. Carson said that you'd be able to do something
since you're a manager of a large company...

00:06:59.771 --> 00:07:01.036
This is bad...

00:07:01.415 --> 00:07:05.230
Mr. Juskin, more of your drunken hillbilly friends?

00:07:06.263 --> 00:07:10.684
I happened upon that Carson guy in
town's bar last year...

00:07:10.719 --> 00:07:13.407
But you really do manage a shipping company?

00:07:14.186 --> 00:07:16.403
I did that for some time, yes.

00:07:21.368 --> 00:07:22.472
Sea-gull!

00:07:22.622 --> 00:07:25.791
Mr. Juskin, Sea-gull is coming!

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.666
We finally have a job!

00:07:32.854 --> 00:07:35.186
Finally, a job after such a long time!
Let's go!

00:07:36.577 --> 00:07:38.339
We don't get to do this too often.

00:07:38.586 --> 00:07:40.523
-Everything okay there?
-Yeah.

00:07:40.824 --> 00:07:44.662
-Mr. Juskin, is this your boat?
-Yeah, you got that right.

00:07:44.683 --> 00:07:48.755
It's a piece of junk even for riding
around the port, let alone going to America...

00:07:49.151 --> 00:07:51.141
Alright! Release brakes!

00:07:53.547 --> 00:07:56.165
I really thought that I'd
get to travel to America.

00:08:12.164 --> 00:08:13.291
That's...

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.386
It's Terry!

00:08:30.617 --> 00:08:35.569
Terry... Terry was playing that melody!
He must have stayed in the port!

00:08:42.727 --> 00:08:43.903
Terry!

00:08:50.551 --> 00:08:52.008
It was you.

00:08:52.134 --> 00:08:54.162
Hello, homeless girl!

00:08:54.346 --> 00:08:56.247
Won't you show me that harmonica?

00:08:56.824 --> 00:08:58.516
Hey, what are you doing?

00:09:00.209 --> 00:09:01.914
It's not Terry's.

00:09:02.251 --> 00:09:05.201
Terry? You know Terry?

00:09:05.492 --> 00:09:06.996
You know him?

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.987
I do. He bought it for me.

00:09:10.289 --> 00:09:11.274
Terry?

00:09:11.497 --> 00:09:13.177
The world is so small!

00:09:13.212 --> 00:09:15.454
Say, won't you tell me about him?

00:09:16.904 --> 00:09:19.135
It was a foggy night, just like this one...

00:09:30.959 --> 00:09:34.463
I couldn't find a job, so I wandered
the streets, looking for dropped coins.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:48.627
Freshly fried...

00:09:49.482 --> 00:09:50.373
Ow!

00:09:52.684 --> 00:09:54.044
Watch where you're going!

00:09:56.569 --> 00:09:58.262
It's my fault though...

00:10:00.146 --> 00:10:01.673
I can manage!

00:10:06.206 --> 00:10:08.914
Boy, is there a cheap hotel around here?

00:10:10.106 --> 00:10:12.009
What, you're searching for a hotel?

00:10:12.456 --> 00:10:15.188
If you need to go around Southampton,
just leave it to Cookie!

00:10:15.989 --> 00:10:17.022
Follow me!

00:10:33.304 --> 00:10:36.091
That was great! I'm so full!

00:10:37.915 --> 00:10:38.856
Cookie, was it?

00:10:39.193 --> 00:10:41.404
Candy will be surprised
when she hears about you.

00:10:41.926 --> 00:10:43.195
Who is this Candy?

00:10:46.201 --> 00:10:48.035
Telling Candy about Cookie...?

00:10:53.858 --> 00:10:56.720
*Denjin Anime Fansub*
The melody Terry is playing is called "Annie Laurie".

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:06.564
That's a nice melody...

00:11:06.992 --> 00:11:09.041
Say, would you let me play it a bit?

00:11:09.327 --> 00:11:10.609
I can't give you this.

00:11:11.138 --> 00:11:12.856
-But just for a minute...
-No.

00:11:18.095 --> 00:11:21.329
I'll go back then.
The dinner was good. Thank you.

00:11:22.683 --> 00:11:25.512
Hey, Cookie.
Do you have a place to stay?

00:11:25.586 --> 00:11:30.791
It's not very comfortable, but I'm
usually sleeping in a warehouse in the port.

00:11:31.465 --> 00:11:34.261
If you want to, you can stay here.

00:11:35.508 --> 00:11:40.590
And tomorrow, I'll buy you a new harmonica.
Until my ship leaves, I'll teach you how to play.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:42.770
Bro!

00:11:44.003 --> 00:11:46.565
And then he bought you this harmonica?

00:11:47.122 --> 00:11:52.535
This one is much better! His harmonica
was smaller and somewhat old.

00:11:53.562 --> 00:11:55.132
Terry!

00:12:08.535 --> 00:12:11.692
I farewelled Terry by playing this harmonica.

00:12:16.325 --> 00:12:18.324
But it sounded so sad.

00:12:22.024 --> 00:12:25.326
I've seen so many people part from each
other in that port.

00:12:30.684 --> 00:12:34.225
He had the face of a man who parts
from someone very dear to him.

00:12:34.642 --> 00:12:37.078
I think her name was Candy.

00:12:50.239 --> 00:12:53.520
So Terry wasn't lonely when he left, wasn't he?

00:12:55.256 --> 00:12:57.612
-Don't tell me you're...
-Candy!

00:13:00.082 --> 00:13:03.882
-What, you were there?
-Mr. Juskin is worried about you!

00:13:04.165 --> 00:13:05.571
I need to go!

00:13:10.445 --> 00:13:12.013
So that's how it was!

00:13:16.796 --> 00:13:18.266
Looks great!

00:13:18.301 --> 00:13:20.472
-Now, Candy, eat up.
-Thank you!

00:13:23.875 --> 00:13:26.033
It's the littlest I could do for you.

00:13:27.647 --> 00:13:29.962
We aren't unemployed anymore.

00:13:30.235 --> 00:13:31.395
You must be hungry!

00:13:31.481 --> 00:13:33.920
But... what about you?

00:13:34.878 --> 00:13:38.639
Don't worry, we're fine just with our drinks.

00:13:38.674 --> 00:13:40.757
And you, Candy, you're like a goddess!

00:13:42.274 --> 00:13:43.479
Goddess?

00:13:43.514 --> 00:13:47.257
Our business has been doing well
ever since you came to us.

00:13:47.638 --> 00:13:51.617
Morever, tomorrow morning, we're doing
our biggest shipping order ever!

00:13:52.056 --> 00:13:55.971
We secured a permanent job...
Looks like we're out of the woods.

00:13:56.917 --> 00:13:59.208
Really, a shipping order to America...

00:13:59.369 --> 00:14:02.056
-Mr. Juskin!
-Don't scare me!

00:14:02.626 --> 00:14:06.836
I'm sorry... tomorrow morning you'll be
shipping a big cargo load to America?

00:14:07.899 --> 00:14:11.834
-That's right...
-Please, put me in the cargo!

00:14:12.767 --> 00:14:17.234
Gotcha...
What? You'd be a stowaway then!

00:14:17.579 --> 00:14:18.989
That's unreasonable!

00:14:19.313 --> 00:14:21.539
First of all, you'd be caught at the customs!

00:14:22.155 --> 00:14:24.458
I want to travel to America as soon as possible!

00:14:25.203 --> 00:14:26.494
Mr. Juskin!

00:14:27.355 --> 00:14:30.335
If they discover her, our business will be ruined!

00:14:31.202 --> 00:14:32.940
I won't cause any trouble!

00:14:39.328 --> 00:14:40.657
I'm begging you!

00:14:46.147 --> 00:14:49.102
Cargo holds on freighters
are cramped and dark.

00:14:49.152 --> 00:14:51.572
Anyhow, it's just like in a tiny box.

00:14:51.904 --> 00:14:52.984
I don't care!

00:14:53.323 --> 00:14:58.712
If you sneak onto a freighter heading to America,
you're in for a whole lot of trouble and pain.

00:14:59.116 --> 00:15:00.226
I can take it!

00:15:00.574 --> 00:15:04.998
You won't have any food or water, and you'll be
trapped in a hot, dark ship's cargo bay.

00:15:06.484 --> 00:15:07.755
Don't do that.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:12.608
Do you have any idea what will those
sailors do to you if they find you?

00:15:12.643 --> 00:15:13.702
I don't care!

00:15:18.417 --> 00:15:20.479
Alright! You depart tomorrow at dawn!

00:15:21.257 --> 00:15:22.557
Thank you!

00:15:23.533 --> 00:15:25.334
That's great, Kurin!

00:15:28.054 --> 00:15:29.074
Have a drink!

00:15:38.185 --> 00:15:42.355
A week has passed since I left St. Paul academy.

00:15:43.665 --> 00:15:47.300
As I write this, I'm at the port in Southampton.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:54.124
Finally, I'll be departing to America
tomorrow at dawn.

00:15:55.179 --> 00:16:03.073
Stear and Archie, excuse my selfishness for leaving
you with nothing but a single letter.

00:16:04.376 --> 00:16:11.366
Annie and Patty, I realized that living a life
where others provide for you isn't right.

00:16:13.256 --> 00:16:17.173
Two men made me realize this fact.

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:23.857
One of them is working in Africa right now.

00:16:29.279 --> 00:16:34.742
The other one ventured on a journey
leaving everything behind himself.

00:16:41.082 --> 00:16:42.882
I am leaving as well.

00:16:43.326 --> 00:16:45.306
To find my own path.

00:16:45.384 --> 00:16:47.050
Please, understand my feelings - -

00:16:48.889 --> 00:16:50.502
You're still awake?

00:16:50.811 --> 00:16:53.336
Yes, I'm almost done writing.

00:16:53.564 --> 00:16:57.145
Tonight is the last time you'll
have a chance of sleeping in a normal bed.

00:16:57.484 --> 00:16:58.483
Yes.

00:16:58.703 --> 00:16:59.916
Candy.

00:17:00.736 --> 00:17:02.632
I'll be praying for you.

00:17:02.913 --> 00:17:05.329
Thank you, mr. Juskin!

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.617
Well, don't catch a cold.
Good night.

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:09.902
Good night!

00:17:12.846 --> 00:17:18.149
Both mr. Carson and mr. Juskin...
They are such good people.

00:17:18.735 --> 00:17:21.001
I'll have to do my best from now on!

00:17:21.475 --> 00:17:23.504
Everyone, I'm so sorry if I saddened you!

00:17:43.497 --> 00:17:47.494
Idiots! You should pretend
like you don't know anything!

00:17:57.272 --> 00:17:59.962
Hurry! You're running late!

00:18:04.161 --> 00:18:05.980
Alright! Untie the ropes!

00:18:11.401 --> 00:18:14.211
Candy, we're finally parting.

00:18:15.932 --> 00:18:18.253
Candy, don't let them find you.

00:18:20.673 --> 00:18:22.096
Be careful.

00:18:22.734 --> 00:18:24.119
Lift it!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:27.067
Take care and don't forget to pray!

00:18:31.647 --> 00:18:32.965
Lift!

00:18:33.127 --> 00:18:36.059
-Winch ok!
-Winch going!

00:18:54.969 --> 00:18:56.200
What's this?

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:02.171
Hey, it says that it's shouldn't
be turned upside-down.

00:19:02.474 --> 00:19:03.975
Okay, let's get it upright then.

00:19:05.803 --> 00:19:08.427
Hey! Don't turn over that crate!

00:19:08.795 --> 00:19:11.340
He's fussing over cargo...

00:19:13.672 --> 00:19:16.088
-That's it...
-How do we carry it then?

00:19:16.452 --> 00:19:17.647
-Hey, let's use this.
-Okay!

00:19:21.706 --> 00:19:24.017
Hey, you heard something?

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:27.205
Come to think of it, it was
like a cry of some animal...

00:19:27.365 --> 00:19:30.460
Aren't you two done yet?
Hurry and put it in the cargo bay!

00:19:31.908 --> 00:19:33.703
Alright, let's go.

00:19:52.364 --> 00:19:54.058
Okay, this is the last one.

00:19:57.149 --> 00:19:59.613
Moving away!

00:20:32.813 --> 00:20:34.949
Candy. Stay well.

00:20:48.485 --> 00:20:53.647
Candy managed to sneak aboard the
freighter ship heading to America.

00:20:56.172 --> 00:21:02.481
However, will she be able to reach America
without anyone discovering her?

00:21:04.665 --> 00:21:09.934
Leaving the shore, the ship ventured
onto the endless, peaceful seas.

00:21:13.356 --> 00:21:19.873
To be continued.
